## 5. Contact configuration

Use empty environment-backed values so missing contact channels can be hidden safely:

```dotenv
SELOTEMNA_PHONE=
SELOTEMNA_WHATSAPP=
SELOTEMNA_EMAIL=
SELOTEMNA_ADDRESS=
SELOTEMNA_BUSINESS_HOURS=
```

Requirements:

- normalise telephone output for `tel:` links;
- build a WhatsApp deep link only from a verified international-format number;
- never render `href="#"`, dummy numbers, sample email addresses or empty contact labels;
- use purple, not WhatsApp green, for the WhatsApp action;
- hide unavailable actions from the header, hero, mobile bar, final CTA and footer.

## 6. Inspection request data contract

### Required fields

- `full_name`
- `telephone`
- `property_interest`
- `preferred_date`
- `consent`

### Optional fields

- `whatsapp`
- `email`
- `preferred_time`
- `message`
- `contact_preference`

### Recommended validation

```text
full_name: required|string|max:120
telephone: required|string|max:30
whatsapp: nullable|string|max:30
email: nullable|email|max:255
property_interest: required|string|max:255
preferred_date: required|date|after_or_equal:today
preferred_time: nullable|in:morning,afternoon,evening,flexible
message: nullable|string|max:2000
contact_preference: nullable|in:phone,whatsapp,email
consent: accepted
```

Persist only the submitted values, `status = new`, and timestamps. Preserve old input after validation failure. After success, display:

> Your inspection request has been received. A Selotemna representative will contact you with the next step.

Do not use “Inspection confirmed.”

## 7. Route plan

```text
GET  /                 home                  HomeController@index
GET  /book-inspection  inspections.create    InspectionRequestController@create
POST /book-inspection  inspections.store     InspectionRequestController@store
```

Until separate public pages exist, homepage navigation should use meaningful section URLs such as `route('home').'#about'`; never use empty `#` links. Use these section IDs:

```text
services
about
properties
diaspora
shortlets
inspection-process
property-support
faq
contact
```

If a service has no valid route or enquiry channel yet, omit its directional link while keeping the informational pathway visible.

## 8. Design-system implementation rules

### Tailwind v4 tokens

Centralise these in the existing top-level `@theme` block:

```css
@theme {
    --font-display: "Sora", "Avenir Next", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    --font-body: "Manrope", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;

    --color-brand-50: #F5F3FA;
    --color-brand-100: #E9E5F5;
    --color-brand-500: #5A4694;
    --color-brand-700: #28166B;
    --color-brand-800: #1C0F4D;
    --color-brand-950: #120933;

    --color-ink-50: #FAFAFB;
    --color-ink-200: #E5E3E8;
    --color-ink-500: #6B6972;
    --color-ink-800: #242329;
    --color-ink-950: #0A0A0B;
}
```

Use Sora for headings and Manrope for body/interface text. Configure both through the existing Laravel Vite font helper. Load only weights actually used.

### Layout

- Standard container: `1280px`
- Wide hero/header container: `1440px`
- Gutters: `20px` mobile, `32px` tablet, `48–64px` desktop
- Standard section padding: `64–80px` mobile and `96–120px` desktop
- Minimum tap target: `44×44px`
- Controls: `10–12px` radius
- Cards/media: `16–20px` radius
- Hero/media frame: `24–28px` radius

### Visual constraints

- Keep approximately 65–70% of the page white/off-white.
- Use purple for primary actions and selected states, not for every surface.
- Use black for structural contrast and the footer.
- No gradients, gold, green accents, glassmorphism, heavy shadows, autoplay carousel, stat strip, floating badges or search bar in the hero.
- Do not wrap every section in cards.
- Use borders, spacing and type hierarchy before shadows.

## 9. Image and logo policy

The supplied logo reference is not a production asset because it contains substantial white canvas. Do not redraw, recolour, stretch or reconstruct the wordmark.

Before production, request:

- transparent PNG or SVG standard logo;
- approved white/reversed logo, if available;
- hero project/property image;
- corporate/about image;
- diaspora/consultation image;
- shortlet image(s);
- construction image;
- property-management image.

During initial implementation:

- create fixed-aspect media slots that render only approved local images;
- when an image is absent, use a clearly non-property branded placeholder that cannot be mistaken for a real listing;
- include explicit replacement notes in code comments;
- never present unrelated stock properties as Selotemna developments;
- do not lazy-load the hero image once supplied;
- lazy-load below-the-fold images and always reserve dimensions.

## 10. Homepage content rules

Use the approved homepage content bundled with `$design-selotemna-web`.

Key copy:

- H1: **Property solutions built around your next move.**
- Primary CTA: **Book an Inspection**
- Secondary CTA: **Explore Properties**
- Inspection submit label: **Request Inspection**

Never render:

- invented property names, locations, prices, specifications or availability;
- fake testimonials, customer photographs, logos or statistics;
- guaranteed returns, appreciation, documentation or titles;
- unverified awards, years of experience or “most trusted” claims;
- bracketed planning placeholders;
- unsupported payment plans or diaspora processes.

Expected initial states:

- properties: approved empty state;
- shortlets: introduction plus safe availability/contact treatment, or no cards;
- testimonials/proof: completely hidden;
- contact actions: conditionally hidden until values exist;
- operating-location SEO: generic until confirmed.

## 11. Accessibility and interaction requirements

- One H1 and logical heading order.
- Semantic `header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `form` and `footer` landmarks.
- Visible labels on all form controls.
- Visible purple focus states with sufficient contrast.
- Normal text contrast of at least `4.5:1`.
- Icon-only controls require accessible names.
- Mobile drawer uses `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, Escape dismissal, backdrop dismissal, focus return and body-scroll locking.
- FAQ triggers are real buttons with `aria-expanded` and controlled panel IDs.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Do not rely on hover for required information.
- Prevent the mobile contact bar from obscuring footer content, form actions or open overlays.

## 12. Verification commands and checks

Run the repository’s own commands rather than inventing alternatives:

```bash
npm run build
php artisan test
./vendor/bin/pint --test
```

Also verify:

- route list contains the named homepage and inspection routes;
- migration runs cleanly;
- homepage returns `200`;
- inspection form rejects missing required values;
- valid request persists once;
- no public square-bracket placeholders exist;
- no dummy `#`, telephone, WhatsApp or email links exist;
- no horizontal overflow at `320px`;
- keyboard navigation works;
- reduced-motion behaviour works;
- desktop, tablet and mobile layouts are visually inspected in a real browser;
- production Vite build emits a manifest and all referenced assets resolve.

